        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Alamgir, Meesha Shafi, Strings, Ali Azmat, Shahzad Hasan\n- Organizations: ARY Digital\n- Products: Music Icons, Aaina\n- Roles: judge, singer-songwriter, musician, actor\n- Topics: Pakistani music, television talent shows, film soundtracks\n\nFacts:\n- In 1976, Alamgir produced the musical album Aaina from the soundtrack of the Urdu-language Pakistani film Aaina.\n- The film Aaina was described as the first ground-breaking and longest-running Urdu-language Pakistani movie of the same name.\n- Ali Azmat was born on April 20, 1970.\n- Ali Azmat is a Pakistani singer-songwriter, musician, and actor.\n- In April 2013, Alamgir joined Meesha Shafi, Strings, Ali Azmat, and Shahzad Hasan as a judge on the singing talent show Music Icons.\n- Music Icons aired on the ARY Digital TV channel.",
